templates.hand_pose:
{style}

The right hand and forearm of a child of about 7, warm light tan skin, not orange, not saturated: a muted, slightly pinkish-beige light brown (midtone about #C49A78, highlights about #D8B894, shadows about #A07A60); a slender, slim hand with long fingers relative to a small, narrow palm (not stubby, not chunky, not toy-like); smooth, simple surfaces with no visible bones, knuckle ridges, tendons or veins, only a soft hint of fingernails; resting on a plain pale worktop. Camera: orthographic top-down view, camera directly overhead looking straight down at the worktop at 90 degrees; we see only the BACK of the hand (palm facing down, against the worktop), never the palm; the forearm lies flat along the worktop and enters from the bottom edge of the frame, pointing up towards the top edge; no horizon, no sides, the hand is not raised or upright. Pose: {pose}. No tool or object in the hand. Sleeve: a plain white linen shirt sleeve, rolled back to between the elbow and the wrist; the forearm is bare below the roll; the soft rolled white linen just shows at the very bottom edge of the frame (or is cropped out); no embroidery, no cuff band, no pattern. This is the master reference hand every other hand pose and reskin is made from. Transparent background: hand and forearm only, with only a faint soft contact shadow where it touches the worktop; no other body parts.

{negative}

