templates.hand_ref_revise:
{style}

Edit the attached reference hand. Keep the camera exactly: orthographic top-down, directly overhead, BACK of the right hand up, palm down on the worktop, forearm lying flat and entering from the bottom edge of the frame. Keep the relaxed pose and the soft lighting. Change: (1) Skin: repaint it as warm light tan skin, not orange, not saturated: a muted, slightly pinkish-beige light brown (midtone about #C49A78, highlights about #D8B894, shadows about #A07A60); the current skin is far too orange. (2) Shape: make the whole hand and forearm slimmer, and make the fingers noticeably longer relative to the palm: a slender, slim hand with long fingers relative to a small, narrow palm (not stubby, not chunky, not toy-like); smooth, simple surfaces with no visible bones, knuckle ridges, tendons or veins, only a soft hint of fingernails. (3) Replace the embroidered kurta cuff entirely. Sleeve: a plain white linen shirt sleeve, rolled back to between the elbow and the wrist; the forearm is bare below the roll; the soft rolled white linen just shows at the very bottom edge of the frame (or is cropped out); no embroidery, no cuff band, no pattern. Transparent background: hand and forearm only, with only a faint soft contact shadow; no other body parts.

{negative}

